{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## Verification evidence\n\n**RED before GREEN, deterministic (AC1).** The polluting ordering was forced rather than\nwaited for:\n\n```\npytest tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/orchestrate/test_main_entry.py \\\n       tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/diffing/test_inbound_removal_confirmation_a4bd.py \\\n       -p no:randomly\nBEFORE: 1 failed, 15 passed  (identical assertion text to the CI -1s on 1715/1716)\nAFTER:  16 passed\n```\n\n`test_main_entry.py` is one instance of the polluter class, not the unique one: any test that\nreaches the reconciler `main()` in-process leaks the level, which is why `--dist worksteal`\nmade shard and run selection look random.\n\n**Guard self-test, both directions and both roots (AC2).**\n`tests/unit/test_caplog_coverage_integrity.py` — 16 passed. The pytester level pair is now\nparametrised over `rebar` and `rebar_reconciler`: without the guard conftest the later INFO\nassertion FAILS (1 passed, 1 failed) on each root; with the guard both pass. So the reconciler\nroot's containment is proven by a red/green pair, not assumed.\n\n**Repeated CI invocation (AC3).** `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/` under\n`-n 3 --dist worksteal --timeout=300`, 10 consecutive runs: **2582 passed every time**\n(210s, 229s, 122s, 114s, 117s, 100s, 109s, 92s, 107s, 93s).\n\n**Full gate set.**\n- `pytest -m \"not integration and not external\" -n 3 --dist worksteal --timeout=300`:\n  12697 passed, 60 skipped.\n- `pytest tests/integration`: 194 passed, 1 skipped.\n- `make lint`, `make typecheck`: clean.\n- Ten `check_*` gates: pass. (`check_complexity_baseline --lock` fails only for want of\n  `GITHUB_REPOSITORY`, a CI-only env var; its `--check` form passes inside `make lint`.)\n- Generators (`gen_adr_index`, `gen_cli_reference`, `gen_env_registry`, `gen_mcp_reference`):\n  no diff.\n\nLanded for review as Gerrit change **1721**, commit `91df0c47d0`."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786614619119643001,"uuid":"4abc3dc8-62ea-442d-a20e-2207abfc7c85"}